**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across TSE open-data pages, CNN/UOL summaries of the Bolsonaro plan, gov.br and Planalto releases, Ministry of Economy and line ministries, BCB, IBGE, Reuters mirrors, and several duplicated wire copies. I kept the most direct ruler-linked documents and dropped duplicates that repeated the same measure, generic macro commentary without a clear Bolsonaro nexus, and out-of-period retrospectives that did not add new 2022 facts. I also found TSE open-data metadata for the proposal PDF, but the ZIP itself was not readable in this environment, so I treated that as discovery only and relied on the CNN summary of the filed plan plus the official registration context. A few gov.br/Planalto pages were blocked by cache or decoding errors when opened, so I used the accessible original pages or their search snippets instead of force-fitting them.

**Remaining gaps**
- A direct readable copy of Bolsonaro's full TSE-filed 2022 plan would strengthen 8B.1 beyond the CNN summary.
- More independent evaluations of whether Renda e Oportunidade, civil-service volunteering, and labor programs changed employment or productivity beyond short-term cash injection would help on 8B.6-8B.8.
- The PPI, tariff-cut, and Plan Safra evidence is mostly official self-report; more third-party implementation/outcome assessments would improve confidence on durable progress.
- Personnel quality and coordination are still only partially evidenced through ministerial delegation and program launches; more on who actually executed the agenda would help.
